{:activity/_scope [{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088517} :activity/id #uuid "79ff03a7-7063-5363-abbf-4b37f65e2992" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048252} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088517 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088890 :tutorial/content "Some important types of matrices have special names.\n\n- An $m \\times n$ matrix in which all entries are zeros is called a **zero matrix**. For example, the following matrices are both zero matrices:\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWe use the notation $O_{m \\times n}$ to represent the zero-matrix with $m$ rows and $n$ columns. So, the zero matrices shown above are $O_{3 \\times 2}$ and $O_{2 \\times 2},$ respectively.\n\n- A $n \\times n$ matrix (meaning the number of rows equals the number of columns) is called a **square matrix**. For example, the following matrices are square matrices of dimensions $2\\times 2$ and $3\\times 3,$ respectively:\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\pi & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\pi \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :tutorial/id #uuid "c2851681-f1a4-52d9-8abc-d07be298cd03" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2982 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "58e8e2e4-2cf1-50c6-b9c4-1ebae7a57b18" :step/math-academy-id 16106 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088518}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088518 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087695 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087502 :question/id #uuid "9c82456c-49ea-5a5e-b0a2-0ab17059acee" :question/math-academy-id "e-4390" :question/problem "Which of the following are zero matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0.1 \\\\ 0.1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "- $P$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a zero matrix since some of its entries are not zeros (for instance, $q_{12}=0.1\\neq0$).\n\n- $R$ is a zero matrix since *all* its entries are zeros.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $R$ are zero matrices."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddb59990-7419-585f-aa1b-901d59c8cfc1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048896}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509675 :question-generator/id #uuid "fd21044d-586d-50a9-b465-bf8c5a806748" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186087695.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a0de8e5-f35c-5259-b1aa-fcd3f1cda78e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$H$, $G$, and $K$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084633} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2bdb16-d36f-5ee0-bc3b-5bdcead4af51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$H$ and $K$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084634} {:answer/id #uuid "0f758d7f-e0c4-5667-af4c-8060b821483a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$H$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084635} {:answer/id #uuid "38ce9a98-c8e9-51a3-a768-7392502b38f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$H$ and $G$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084636} {:answer/id #uuid "4945cdd8-a97c-5875-8405-b8cbf0357598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$K$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084637}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084636} :answer-field/id #uuid "977664f3-2676-598f-b147-27d142e675a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084632}] :question/id #uuid "8208c8d