ty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c0fa1b96-0701-5539-993f-8523f6af2e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-68745" :question/problem "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $S$ is a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. Also, all the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nNotice that $S$ is not an identity matrix since the diagonal entries are not all ones.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a diagonal matrix since it's not a square matrix.\n\n- $Y$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. But some of the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are not zeros (for instance, ${y}_{31}=1\\ne 0$).\n\nTherefore, only $S$ is a diagonal matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186568918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a117d47f-5218-5d82-82e9-ffcf370c0559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569004} {:answer/id #uuid "bf860344-eec5-56e2-88c2-3d436b9ef657" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569022}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569022} :answer-field/id #uuid "0918ebc1-241e-57b0-a7b8-ffeaf8e948af" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfe29f00-601a-59c2-b837-432d3e7573a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569046} {:answer/id #